# {{name}}

A juiz component written in Zig. It was made with `juiz pkg create --idl` of juiz {{juiz_version}},
from the process / container declarations of `{{idl_main}}`.

License: {{license}}

## What is inside

{{types_table}}

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `{{idl_main}}` | The types and the declarations (JIDL) |
| `src/{{name}}.zig` | The Component. Each function is a type, listed in `juiz.exportComponent` at the end. Write the bodies (`return error.NotImplemented`) |
| `build.zig` | Generates the Zig types of the `.jidl` (`juiz.addTypes`), builds the plugin `lib{{name}}` with zigjuiz, and puts it with libjuiz_sdk in `zig-out/plugins/` |
| `build.zig.zon` | The Zig package. It points to zigjuiz (the Zig library of juiz) |
| `app/app.conf` | The configuration to start juiz with. It is also the entry of the `.juizapp` package |
| `app/juizapp.yaml` | The `.juizapp` manifest (name, version, required juiz version) |
| `scripts/dev.sh` | Build the plugin and put it with libjuiz_sdk in `app/plugins/<target>/` (`--target` for another machine) |
| `scripts/pack.sh` | Build in release mode and make `dist/{{name}}-<version>.juizapp` |

## Requirements

Linux or macOS. This skeleton does not support Windows yet (juiz issue #588).

- juiz {{juiz_version}} (`juiz --version`). Install it with `cargo install juiz_app --version {{juiz_version}}` or `pip install juiz-cli=={{juiz_version}}`
- Zig 0.17.x ([ziglang.org](https://ziglang.org/download/), or `pip install ziglang==0.17.1` and `ZIG="python3 -m ziglang" scripts/dev.sh`).
  zigjuiz supports only this version of Zig
- `juiz-idl` or `juiz` in PATH: the build generates the types with `juiz-idl -g zig` (or `juiz idl -g zig`)
- libjuiz_sdk {{juiz_version}} in `{{juiz_sdk_dir}}`. Install it with `juiz sdk install` (`juiz sdk path` prints where it is)
- The juiz source of {{juiz_version}} for zigjuiz, in `{{zigjuiz_dir}}`
- zigjuiz {{juiz_version}}, the Zig library of juiz. `scripts/dev.sh` adds it to `build.zig.zon` the first time (it needs the network once):
  `zig fetch --save=zigjuiz {{zigjuiz_fetch}}`

`build.zig.zon` points to zigjuiz with the path `{{zigjuiz_path}}`, relative to this directory (Zig does not take an absolute path there).
If you move this project or zigjuiz, change the path in `build.zig.zon`.

zigjuiz and libjuiz_sdk must be the same version as juiz: juiz does not load a plugin that carries another version of libjuiz_sdk.
`app/juizapp.yaml` requires `juiz: "={{juiz_version}}"` for the same reason.
When you update juiz, get zigjuiz and libjuiz_sdk of the new version, and change `build.zig.zon` and `app/juizapp.yaml`.
To use libjuiz_sdk in another directory, run `JUIZ_SDK_DIR=<dir> scripts/dev.sh` (or `zig build -Djuiz-sdk=<dir>`).

## Write, build, run and call

